      "FLORENCE: Don't worry -- she'll get used to it.\nCHARLOTTE: Disappoint me? Why, what do you mean, dear?",
      "CHARLOTTE: I'd love to, at any time.\nFLORENCE: Well, I'm a woman who craves nourishment. Let's ankle out of here and find a beanery. Come on, Moon-struck. Let's get going.\nCHARLOTTE: We'll be coming to the opening.",
      "FLORENCE: Listen, Kid, I'm going to leave you flat. I just thought of something and I've got to get to the office.\nCHARLOTTE: But what about lunch?\nFLORENCE: I'll have it for supper. So long.",
      "CHARLOTTE: I think so.\nFLORENCE: Well, thank goodness, that's settled."
    ]
